WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
RANK behaves like a competition ranking.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:07.182
If two employees tie for second, both receive rank two.

00:00:07.182 --> 00:00:09.362
The next rank is four.

00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:14.887
This is useful when the numeric rank should reflect positions consumed by the tie.

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:18.967
Ranking functions differ mainly in how they handle ties.

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:26.072
ROW_NUMBER forces a unique sequence, RANK leaves gaps after ties, and DENSE_RANK does not.

00:00:26.072 --> 00:00:29.792
Add deterministic tie-breakers when a unique order matters;

00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:34.080
otherwise two executions can choose different rows among tied values.
